Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0200
Subject: Sound: open the audio device in the host's byte order (AUDIO_S16SYS)

snd_init asked SDL_audiolib for AUDIO_S16, which in SDL2 is AUDIO_S16LSB:
little-endian samples whatever the host. That is correct on a big-endian
host too (SDL_audiolib converts its float mix with floatToS16LSB, and SDL
or the sound server swaps the bytes back), but on the PS3's PPE every
sample is then swapped twice: once into little-endian by the mixer and
once back by whoever feeds the big-endian sound hardware. AUDIO_S16SYS is
the same 16-bit signed format in native order (AUDIO_S16LSB on x86, so
nothing changes there); SDL_audiolib handles AUDIO_S16MSB already
(floatToS16MSB).

Forwarded: no

--- a/Source/engine/sound.cpp
+++ b/Source/engine/sound.cpp
@@ -212,9 +212,9 @@
 	gbMusicOn = *sgOptions.Audio.musicVolume > VOLUME_MIN;
 
 	// Initialize the SDL_audiolib library. Set the output sample rate to
-	// 22kHz, the audio format to 16-bit signed, use 2 output channels
+	// 22kHz, the audio format to 16-bit signed in the host's byte order, use 2 output channels
 	// (stereo), and a 2KiB output buffer.
-	if (!Aulib::init(*sgOptions.Audio.sampleRate, AUDIO_S16, *sgOptions.Audio.channels, *sgOptions.Audio.bufferSize, *sgOptions.Audio.device)) {
+	if (!Aulib::init(*sgOptions.Audio.sampleRate, AUDIO_S16SYS, *sgOptions.Audio.channels, *sgOptions.Audio.bufferSize, *sgOptions.Audio.device)) {
 		LogError(LogCategory::Audio, "Failed to initialize audio (Aulib::init): {}", SDL_GetError());
 		return;
 	}
